# Print-temp leak class, view-source shape: `s.trim()` returns a cap=0
# VIEW into `s` — the printf materialization copies the 32-byte view
# struct (no heap), and `gorget_string_free` no-ops on cap=0. Pins that
# registering print temps unconditionally is safe for views: no
# double-free of the source's heap, output unchanged.
void main():
    String s = "  padded  "
    print(s.trim())
    print(f"[{s.trim()}]")
    print(s.len())
